# Living Survey: Quantum_Computing                                                                                   
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Introduction                                                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Quantum_Computing**.                                    
                                                                                                                     

New content:                                                                                                         

                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Algorithms & Software Ecosystem                                                                           
                                                                                                                     
Recent studies have expanded the software landscape and algorithmic understanding of quantum systems. Developer      
engagement analysis reveals that hybrid quantum-classical computing and circuit implementation dominate community    
discussions, with Qiskit and Q-sharp being the most referenced toolchains alongside Grover's and Shor's algorithms   
`[^https:__openalex.org_W7155247427]`. In the domain of materials and spin dynamics, PULSEE introduces an open-source
Python framework bridging quantum information science and magnetic resonance spectroscopy, enabling precise          
simulation of spin time evolution and quantum gates `[^10.1016_j.cpc.2022.108598]`. Furthermore, comprehensive       
reviews continue to map the prospective applications and stakeholder impacts of quantum computing, emphasizing       
superposition and entanglement as foundational paradigms `[^10.5120_ijca2021921834]`.                                
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Cryptography & Communication Networks                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
Secure communication remains a primary driver for quantum research. A detailed Python simulation of the BB84 QKD     
protocol has been published, modeling state preparation, Born rule measurements, intercept-resend eavesdropping, and 
classical post-processing stages like sifting and privacy amplification `[^10.6084_m9.figshare.32051724]`. Parallel  
theoretical work explores novel approaches to quantum cryptography, detailing protocols like BB84, B92, and B91,     
alongside Shor's algorithm implementation and security against photon-splitting and faked-state attacks              
`[^https:__openalex.org_W7112574406]`. The broader infrastructure vision is captured in primers on the quantum       
internet, which outline its theoretical foundations, ultra-secure connectivity potential, and the transition from    
classical to quantum state-based information transmission `[^10.31695_ijerat.2025.9.1]`.                             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Computing Applications & Simulations                                                                      
                                                                                                                     
Quantum computing is increasingly applied to complex classical simulation problems. Reviews on computational fluid   
dynamics (CFD) discuss quantum algorithms for Navier-Stokes equations, Lattice Boltzmann methods, and analog quantum 
simulations tailored for aeronautical heat exchangers `[^10.11159_icffts23.133]` `[^10.21741_9781644902813-38]`. In  
materials science, practical guides demonstrate applying quantum annealing to calculate the relative energy of       
defective graphene structures, translating chemical models directly to qubit representations `[^10.1063_5.0151346]`. 
Additionally, hybrid granular computing approaches have been proposed for quantum genetic optimization, utilizing    
digital computers for fitness evaluation and quantum processors for population evolution to tackle continuous        
optimization problems `[^10.1007_s41066-022-00348-9]`.                                                               
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Quantum Hardware, Architectures & Future Trends                                                                   
                                                                                                                     
Architectural innovations continue to challenge classical scaling limits. A unified framework redefining matter and  
energy introduces "atom computing," where controlled electron and photonic flows replace transistors to enable       
deterministic switching beyond qubit-based constraints `[^10.34257_gjsfra257362]`. Comparative studies contextualize 
quantum computing's performance potential against traditional digital and biological architectures, providing        
standardized models for industry adoption `[^10.1109_mc.2021.3083430]`. Market and development trends are also being 
tracked through open-source repositories and financial news, highlighting the intersection of software development   
and economic sentiment in quantum technology adoption `[^10.1007_978-3-031-90727-2_20]`.                             
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
## Post-Quantum Cryptography & Security                                                                              
                                                                                                                     
